{#- embed-panel.njk — the "As embedded" half of one section

   Included THREE TIMES on the ministry page, once per section, so everything
   inside is addressed by data-emb WITHIN the panel rather than by id. Ids
   would collide the moment the second one rendered.

   Read one way it is a preview; read the other it is the "hide the visualiser
   and just edit the data" control. Same switch, one job.

   The caller sets `embedWidget` to roadmap | goal | prayer. There is no widget
   picker: the section has already chosen.  -#}

<div class="emb-bar" data-embed-panel data-widget="{{ embedWidget }}" hidden>

  {#- Two buttons, not a checkbox: this chooses between two views, and a tick
     box would imply the second is an addition to the first. -#}
  <div class="emb-views" role="tablist" aria-label="View">
    <button type="button" class="emb-view is-on" role="tab" aria-selected="true"
            data-emb="viewEdit" data-i18n="emb.viewEdit">Edit</button>
    <button type="button" class="emb-view" role="tab" aria-selected="false"
            data-emb="viewEmbed" data-i18n="emb.viewEmbed">As embedded</button>
  </div>

  {#- Whether this is on somebody else's site RIGHT NOW — the question you
     actually have while looking at either view. -#}
  <span class="emb-state" data-emb="state"></span>
</div>

<section class="emb-panel" data-emb="panel" hidden>

  <div class="emb-stagebar">
    <p class="emb-lede" data-i18n="{{ 'emb.ledeRoadmap' if embedWidget == 'roadmap' else ('emb.ledePrayer' if embedWidget == 'prayer' else 'emb.ledeGoal') }}">
      This is exactly what somebody sees when they put it on their own site.
    </p>

    {#- DESKTOP OR MOBILE. The widget chooses its layout from the width it is
       actually given, not from a media query — so narrowing the frame is not
       a simulation of a phone, it is the same decision a phone would cause.
       The roadmap is a different thing at each width: a horizontal rail or a
       vertical column. -#}
    <div class="emb-devices" role="tablist" aria-label="Width">
      <button type="button" class="emb-device is-on" role="tab" aria-selected="true"
              data-emb="devWide" data-i18n="emb.desktop">Desktop</button>
      <button type="button" class="emb-device" role="tab" aria-selected="false"
              data-emb="devNarrow" data-i18n="emb.mobile">Mobile</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="emb-stage" data-emb="stage">
    <iframe data-emb="frame" title="Embed preview" sandbox="allow-scripts"></iframe>
  </div>

  <div class="emb-controls">
    <label class="emb-field">
      <span data-i18n="emb.accent">Accent</span>
      <span class="emb-colour">
        <input type="color" data-emb="accent" value="#6D4AFF">
        <input type="text" data-emb="accentHex" class="emb-hex" maxlength="7"
               spellcheck="false" aria-label="Accent colour hex">
      </span>
    </label>

    {#- Left on "match automatically" it is derived from the first by rotating
       the hue — the relationship cyan and seafoam have on chaseroush.com.
       Turning it off hands the pair over entirely. -#}
    <label class="emb-field">
      <span data-i18n="emb.accent2">Second colour</span>
      <span class="emb-colour">
        <input type="color" data-emb="accent2" value="#0AFFA2">
        <input type="text" data-emb="accent2Hex" class="emb-hex" maxlength="7"
               spellcheck="false" aria-label="Second colour hex">
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="emb-field emb-auto">
      <span data-i18n="emb.pairAuto">Match it</span>
      <span class="emb-checkline">
        <input type="checkbox" data-emb="pairAuto" checked>
        <span data-i18n="emb.pairAutoNote">automatically</span>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="emb-field">
      <span data-i18n="emb.theme">Background</span>
      <select data-emb="theme">
        <option value="auto" data-i18n="emb.auto">Match their page</option>
        <option value="light" data-i18n="emb.light">Always light</option>
        <option value="dark" data-i18n="emb.dark">Always dark</option>
      </select>
    </label>

    <label class="emb-field">
      <span data-i18n="emb.lang">Language</span>
      <select data-emb="lang"></select>
    </label>
  </div>

  {#- Only the roadmap is drawn against a period. -#}
  {% if embedWidget == "roadmap" %}
  <div class="emb-period">
    <div class="emb-period-text">
      <h4 data-i18n="emb.periodTitle">The period this covers</h4>
      <p data-i18n="emb.periodDesc">Set both and the roadmap is drawn against these dates, with the line filling as time passes. Leave them empty and it spans your milestones instead — which means the last one always sits at the end.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="emb-period-fields">
      <label class="emb-field">
        <span data-i18n="emb.periodStart">Starts</span>
        <input type="date" data-emb="tlStart">
      </label>
      <label class="emb-field">
        <span data-i18n="emb.periodEnd">Ends</span>
        <input type="date" data-emb="tlEnd">
      </label>
      <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" data-emb="tlSave" data-i18n="emb.periodSave">Save period</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <p class="emb-shared" data-i18n="emb.sharedNote">
    Colours are shared by every widget this ministry publishes. The language
    belongs to this snippet only.
  </p>

  {#- THE PUBLICATION DECISION, worded as what it does rather than as a setting
     name. Everything above works whether this is on or off, because you should
     be able to look before you decide. -#}
  <div class="emb-publish">
    <div class="emb-publish-text">
      <h4 data-i18n="emb.shareTitle">Let other websites show this</h4>
      <p data-emb="shareDesc" data-i18n="emb.shareOff">
        Nobody can use the code below yet.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="emb-publish-ctl">
      <button type="button" class="switch" role="switch" aria-checked="false" data-emb="on">
        <span class="switch-track"><span class="switch-state" data-emb="onState">Off</span><span class="switch-knob"></span></span>
      </button>
      <p class="rolegate" data-emb="notAdmin" hidden data-i18n="emb.adminOnly">
        An administrator changes this.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  {#- TWO THINGS TO COPY, for different people: the snippet for whoever wants
     the picture, the data address for whoever is building their own. -#}
  <div class="emb-copies">
    <div class="emb-copy">
      <div class="emb-copy-head">
        <h4 data-i18n="emb.snippetTitle">The code to paste</h4>
        <p data-i18n="emb.snippetDesc">For anyone who just wants the picture on their page.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="emb-codewrap">
        <pre class="emb-code" data-emb="code"></pre>
        <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" data-emb="copyCode" data-i18n="common.copy">Copy</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="emb-copy">
      <div class="emb-copy-head">
        <h4 data-i18n="emb.apiTitle">The data behind it</h4>
        <p data-i18n="emb.apiDesc">For anyone building their own design. Plain JSON, same numbers, no key needed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="emb-codewrap">
        <pre class="emb-code" data-emb="api"></pre>
        <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" data-emb="copyApi" data-i18n="common.copy">Copy</button>
      </div>
      <a class="emb-guide" data-emb="guide" download>
        <span data-i18n="emb.guide">Download the developer guide</span>
        <span class="emb-guide-sub" data-i18n="emb.guideSub">Markdown — how to read the data, and how to keep working when goals or milestones are added.</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

</section>
